# img, the editor of Icon image strings (ipl_gprogs): pick button colours on the palette, paint cells and drags with the left and right buttons,
# label the palette, take a colour from a cell with a shifted click, replace one colour by another, write the image string, quit (which writes
# it again). The window is 500 by 300; cell j i of the 16 by 16 grid stands at 205+15j 30+15i; the palette is the block at the left.
# the left button takes red from the palette
click 1 65 87
wait
click 1 212 37
wait
drag 1 242 67 332 67
wait
# the right button takes blue
click 3 65 228
wait
drag 3 302 97 302 187
wait
# L labels the palette
key L
wait
# a shifted middle click on the first cell gives the middle button that cell's red
keydown Shift_L
click 2 212 37
keyup Shift_L
wait
click 2 407 232
wait
# R turns every cell of the right button's colour into the left button's
key R
wait
# W writes the image string; Q writes it again and ends the program
key W
key Q
